<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" version="2.0"><channel><title>RSS: Album Reviews</title><description>Album Reviews content RSS feed</description><link>https://pitchfork.com</link><atom:link href="https://pitchfork.com/feed/feed-album-reviews/rss" rel="self" type="application/atom+xml"/><copyright>© Condé Nast 2026</copyright><language>en-US</language><lastBuildDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 14:00:02 +0000</lastBuildDate><item><title>Radical Frame</title><link>https://pitchfork.com/reviews/albums/actress-radical-frame/</link><guid isPermaLink="false">6aabc6884a0b58532218bba6</guid><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 04:03:00 +0000</pubDate><media:content/><description>Depressive electro epics, mangled bursts of spoken word, self-destructing rap anthems: The UK avant-techno producer sounds unusually prickly on his 10th album.</description><category>Reviews / Albums</category><dc:creator>Andrew Ryce</dc:creator><dc:publisher>Condé Nast</dc:publisher><media:thumbnail url="https://media.pitchfork.com/photos/6aa86b3aae3e28fd3939c15d/master/pass/5054429207088.jpg" width="6000" height="6000"/></item><item><title>Fell Asleep in the Sun</title><link>https://pitchfork.com/reviews/albums/after-fell-asleep-in-the-sun/</link><guid isPermaLink="false">6ab1628af99f7bf88c241c6e</guid><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 04:02:00 +0000</pubDate><media:content/><description>The Los Angeles band’s note-perfect reverence for 2000s trip-hop, soft rock, and breakbeat pop makes for a superficially pretty but frustratingly shallow debut LP.</description><category>Reviews / Albums</category><dc:creator>Billie Bugara</dc:creator><dc:publisher>Condé Nast</dc:publisher><media:thumbnail url="https://media.pitchfork.com/photos/6ab16233882ead5224eb3311/master/pass/After%20-%20Fell%20Asleep%20in%20the%20Sun%20album%20art.jpg" width="1400" height="1400"/></item><item><title>I Lost My Way for Centuries</title><link>https://pitchfork.com/reviews/albums/the-drin-i-lost-my-way-for-centuries/</link><guid isPermaLink="false">6ab14a2c06bd4642732cce09</guid><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 04:01:00 +0000</pubDate><media:content/><description>On a sprawling yet accessible double album that trades murky electronics for mostly analog instruments, Dylan McCartney and co. inject record-collector touchstones with a contemporary sense of unease.</description><category>Reviews / Albums</category><dc:creator>Stuart Berman</dc:creator><dc:publisher>Condé Nast</dc:publisher><media:thumbnail url="https://media.pitchfork.com/photos/6ab149d316371b41ccca52ba/master/pass/The%20Drin-I%20Lost%20My%20Way%20for%20Centuries.jpg" width="3000" height="3000"/></item></channel></rss>